<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">In the profiles</h2><ul class="yr-prof"><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/south-yemen"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/South%20Yemen.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>South Yemen</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The NLF begins its armed uprising in the Radfan mountains</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/malaysia"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Malaysia.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Malaysia</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Malaysia is proclaimed on 16 September; Indonesia steps up its Confrontation</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/sultanate-of-zanzibar"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Sultanate%20of%20Zanzibar.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Sultanate of Zanzibar</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Zanzibar becomes independent under Sultan Jamshid bin Abdullah</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/religion/bahai-faith"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Bah%C3%A1'%C3%AD%20Faith.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Bahá'í Faith</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Universal House of Justice, the faith’s governing body, is elected for the first time</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/civil-rights-movement"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Civil%20rights%20movement.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Civil rights movement</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Birmingham campaign and the March on Washington, where King speaks of his dream</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/pan-africanism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Pan-Africanism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Pan-Africanism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Thirty-two independent states found the Organisation of African Unity in Addis Ababa</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/syrian-arab-republic"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Syrian%20Arab%20Republic.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Syrian Arab Republic</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">On 8 March the Military Committee of the Arab Socialist Ba'ath Party seizes power and establishes a one-party state under martial law.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/socialist-federal-republic-of-yugoslavia"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Socialist%20Federal%20Republic%20of%20Yugoslavia.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Socialist Federal Republic of Yugoslavia</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">A new constitution renames the state the Socialist Federal Republic of Yugoslavia; emigration of workers is legalised and Western travel opens.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/culture/longshan-culture"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Longshan%20culture.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Longshan culture</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Kwang-chih Chang describes a uniform “Longshanoid horizon”, which he replaces in 1986 with a “Chinese interaction sphere” of regional cultures</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/feminism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Feminism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Feminism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Betty Friedan’s The Feminine Mystique sparks the beginning of second-wave feminism in the United States</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/life/haile-selassie"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Haile%20Selassie.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Haile Selassie</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">He presides over the formation of the Organisation of African Unity and is elected its first chairperson</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/kingdom-of-cambodia-1953-1970"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kingdom%20of%20Cambodia%20(1953-1970).png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kingdom of Cambodia (1953-1970)</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Sihanouk nationalises banking, foreign trade and insurance and ends the United States aid programme</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-vietnam"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20Vietnam.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of Vietnam</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Huế Phật Đản shootings of 8 May set off the Buddhist crisis, and on 1 November Diệm is overthrown and killed in a coup led by General Dương Văn Minh</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/seoul"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Seoul.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Seoul</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Two annexations more than double the size of the city</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/benin-city"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Benin%20City.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Benin City</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Benin City becomes the capital of the Mid-Western Region</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/addis-ababa"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Addis%20Ababa.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Addis Ababa</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Organisation of African Unity is formed and keeps its headquarters in the city</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/lascaux"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Lascaux.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Lascaux</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The cave closes to visitors after lichen and crystals appear on the walls, and the paintings are restored</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/gobekli-tepe"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/G%C3%B6bekli%20Tepe.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Göbekli Tepe</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">A survey directed by Halet Çambel and Robert John Braidwood first noted the site</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/life/martin-luther-king-jr"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Martin%20Luther%20King%20Jr..png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Martin Luther King Jr.</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Writes the Letter from Birmingham Jail and delivers the I Have a Dream speech at the March on Washington</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/prague-spring"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Prague%20Spring.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Prague Spring</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Marxist intellectuals organise the Liblice Conference on Franz Kafka, which marks the start of the cultural democratisation of Czechoslovakia</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/wahhabism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Wahhabism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Wahhabism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Saudi clergy expel the scholar al-Albani after a fatwa on women's faces</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/trotskyism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Trotskyism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Trotskyism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The International Secretariat and some sections of the International Committee reunify</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/baathism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Ba'athism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Ba'athism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Military Committee of the Syrian Ba'ath party launches a coup that sets up a one-party state in Syria</span></li></ul></section>
